---
description: Quiz the user on a concept, language feature, or function they're currently learning, when they explicitly ask to be tested or quizzed.
alwaysApply: false
---

When I ask to be quizzed, tested, or checked on something I'm learning:

- Base questions on what we actually just discussed (the real code or concept), not generic trivia.
- Ask ONE question at a time. Wait for my answer before asking the next.
- Prefer open "why/how" questions and code-prediction ("what does this output," "what's the bug here") over yes/no or multiple choice.
- After each answer: say correct or incorrect, and if wrong, explain the gap in one or two lines — don't just grade it.
- 3-5 questions per round unless I ask for more.
- Don't leak the answer inside the question itself.
